# This app has no database, no session store and no server-side model key.
# Every model call is made from the browser with the reader's own OAuth token,
# so there is very little to configure. Both variables below are optional.

# Gemini's token endpoint requires a client_secret alongside the PKCE code.
# gemini-cli is a public desktop client, so its secret is published rather than
# confidential, and the SDK ships that published value — the app works without
# setting this. Set it only to pin a different one; the proxy appends it to
# form-urlencoded POSTs bound for Google (lib/oauth/proxy.ts).
# GEMINI_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Set to 1 to build the /demo variant, which serves the app under a basePath
# of /demo with assets at /demo-assets (next.config.ts). Leave unset for a
# deployment that owns its own domain.
# IS_DEMO=1
